00:02:14.685 --> 00:02:18.335
when you handle those
hard things close at hand,

00:02:18.335 --> 00:02:22.019
making those hard decisions right now

00:02:22.019 --> 00:02:23.834
that you don't want to make,

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:27.853
learning those things
that you don't like to do,

00:02:27.853 --> 00:02:29.177
but you know that in order for you

00:02:29.177 --> 00:02:30.952
to get where you want to go,

00:02:30.952 --> 00:02:34.327
this is one of the hoops that
you have to flip through.

00:02:34.327 --> 00:02:36.862
And I'm saying to you,
whatever you got to do, do it,

00:02:36.862 --> 00:02:38.067
because if you don't,

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:41.717
life is going to whoop you
until you surrender and say,

00:02:41.717 --> 00:02:43.730
"Okay, all right, all
right, all right, all right.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.682
"I'll cooperate, okay.

00:02:44.682 --> 00:02:46.103
"I'll learn, okay."

00:02:46.103 --> 00:02:49.067
It had to wear me out a long time.

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:51.252
So if it's hard, then do it hard.

00:02:51.252 --> 00:02:53.643
You're going to focus
to develop your skills.

00:02:53.643 --> 00:02:55.959
A guy was, was um,

00:02:55.959 --> 00:02:58.152
the new owner of a team,

00:02:58.152 --> 00:03:02.211
a baseball team that was in
the basement of the league

00:03:02.211 --> 00:03:03.566
when he took it over.

00:03:03.566 --> 00:03:04.399
He went to the pitcher

00:03:04.399 --> 00:03:06.051
and he said, "What is your best throw?"

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:07.726
And he said, "Well, I got a good curveball

00:03:07.726 --> 00:03:09.543
"and I've got a good fastball."

00:03:09.543 --> 00:03:11.355
And he went on talking
about his different throws.

00:03:11.355 --> 00:03:12.925
He said, "But tell me this.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:15.825
"What is your best throw?"

00:03:15.825 --> 00:03:17.900
He thought for a moment.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.458
He said, "I've got a good fastball."

00:03:20.458 --> 00:03:22.965
He said, "That's all
I want you to work on.

00:03:22.965 --> 00:03:23.874
"Nothing else.

00:03:23.874 --> 00:03:26.028
"Just develop your fastball."

00:03:26.028 --> 00:03:29.461
The next year, they went
to the World Series.

00:03:29.461 --> 00:03:33.192
Most people don't know
what their fastball is.

00:03:33.192 --> 00:03:35.091
Most people go through life

00:03:35.091 --> 00:03:38.282
never discovering what their talents are.

00:03:38.282 --> 00:03:40.998
Most people never develop their talents.

00:03:40.998 --> 00:03:42.657
They have skills and abilities,

00:03:42.657 --> 00:03:44.257
but if you don't nurture them,

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.492
if you don't develop them,

00:03:45.492 --> 00:03:46.979
they will never serve you.

00:03:46.979 --> 00:03:49.082
Your gifts can take you many places

00:03:49.082 --> 00:03:51.665
if you develop your gifts.

00:03:51.665 --> 00:03:52.814
Most of us don't like to do

00:03:52.814 --> 00:03:56.089
those things that come easy to us.

00:03:56.089 --> 00:03:57.982
I've always loved to talk to people.

00:03:57.982 --> 00:03:59.876
I decided, taking this advice,

00:03:59.876 --> 00:04:03.265
to develop my skills as a speaker,

00:04:03.265 --> 00:04:06.291
and my gift has developed and developed

00:04:06.291 --> 00:04:09.239
and has taken me many places.

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:12.248
You have something that you
brought to the universe,

00:04:12.248 --> 00:04:14.146
and that if you decide that my life

00:04:14.146 --> 00:04:17.813
deserves my developing
this, what I do well,

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.855
and becoming the best at
it and mastering myself

00:04:21.855 --> 00:04:24.637
and seeing what I have within me.

00:04:24.637 --> 00:04:28.705
If you decide to drop
your buckets where you are

00:04:28.705 --> 00:04:30.622
and develop your gifts,

00:04:31.679 --> 00:04:35.228
I grant you you'll never ever be without.

00:04:35.228 --> 00:04:38.163
I grant you your gifts
will take you places

00:04:38.163 --> 00:04:40.611
that will literally amaze you.

00:04:40.611 --> 00:04:45.459
I grant you that if you begin
to work to develop your gifts,

00:04:45.459 --> 00:04:47.834
you'll develop a strong
sense of happiness.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.237
You'll get a larger vision of yourself,

00:04:49.237 --> 00:04:50.929
because part of beginning to get

00:04:50.929 --> 00:04:52.262
a larger vision of yourself,

00:04:52.262 --> 00:04:54.745
all of us need some area of our lives

00:04:54.745 --> 00:04:58.744
where we can have a feeling of competence.

00:04:58.744 --> 00:05:00.828
People know when they
think about this area,

00:05:00.828 --> 00:05:02.828
that's something you do.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:07.287
That you eat and sleep that.

00:05:07.287 --> 00:05:08.560
And that you do that.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.127
You do that.

00:05:10.127 --> 00:05:11.516
And people know it.

00:05:11.516 --> 00:05:12.461
And you know it,

00:05:12.461 --> 00:05:14.694
and you know that you
know that you know this.

00:05:14.694 --> 00:05:17.085
If you don't know anything
else, you know this.

00:05:17.085 --> 00:05:17.918
(laughter)

00:05:17.918 --> 00:05:19.454
Can you tell I know I know what I'm doing?

