(laughter)
Ah, hello. (laughs)

00:05:22.268 --> 00:05:23.838
You know this.

00:05:23.838 --> 00:05:25.636
So you've got to work on it.

00:05:25.636 --> 00:05:26.611
Dr. Howard Thurman,

00:05:26.611 --> 00:05:29.626
one of the mentors of Dr.
Martin Luther King, Jr.

00:05:29.626 --> 00:05:32.963
and Albert Schweitzer and Mahatma Gandhi.

00:05:32.963 --> 00:05:34.247
He was a very brilliant writer.

00:05:34.247 --> 00:05:36.144
He wrote some things
that really grabbed me.

00:05:36.144 --> 00:05:39.441
He wrote "Deep is the Hunger,"

00:05:39.441 --> 00:05:41.843
"The Voice of the Genuine,"

00:05:41.843 --> 00:05:43.119
"The Centering Moment."

00:05:43.119 --> 00:05:47.130
During the time after receiving
238 radiation seed implants,

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.202
I was reflecting on his words,

00:05:49.202 --> 00:05:52.941
and these words kept me up that night.

00:05:52.941 --> 00:05:57.108
He said, "The ideal situation
for a man or woman to die

00:05:57.993 --> 00:06:00.511
"is to have family
members praying with them

00:06:00.511 --> 00:06:02.261
"as they cross over."

00:06:03.775 --> 00:06:07.817
He said, "But imagine if you
will, being on your deathbed,

00:06:07.817 --> 00:06:09.915
"and standing around your bed,

00:06:09.915 --> 00:06:11.998
"the ghost of the dreams,

00:06:12.856 --> 00:06:14.389
"the ideas,

00:06:14.389 --> 00:06:15.791
"the abilities,

00:06:15.791 --> 00:06:19.107
"the talents given to
you by life and that you,

00:06:19.107 --> 00:06:23.790
"for whatever reason, you
never went after that dream,

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.892
"you never acted on those ideas,

00:06:25.892 --> 00:06:27.618
"you never used those talents,

00:06:27.618 --> 00:06:29.505
"you never used those gifts.

00:06:29.505 --> 00:06:31.483
"And there they are
standing around your bed,

00:06:31.483 --> 00:06:34.533
"looking at you with
large, angry eyes, saying,

00:06:34.533 --> 00:06:35.866
"We came to you,

00:06:36.791 --> 00:06:41.032
"and only you could have
given us life, and now

00:06:41.032 --> 00:06:43.615
"we must die with you forever."

00:06:45.482 --> 00:06:48.056
(crowd murmurs)

00:06:48.056 --> 00:06:50.289
And the question is,

00:06:50.289 --> 00:06:51.789
if you died today,

00:06:52.705 --> 00:06:53.705
what dreams,

00:06:55.647 --> 00:06:56.564
what ideas,

00:06:57.638 --> 00:06:59.015
what talents, what books,

00:06:59.015 --> 00:07:00.756
what music, what leadership,

00:07:00.756 --> 00:07:03.173
what voice will die with you?

00:07:04.248 --> 00:07:06.888
Myles Munroe, great orator and speaker,

00:07:06.888 --> 00:07:08.664
said the wealthiest place on the planet,

00:07:08.664 --> 00:07:10.635
it's not in the Far East where
there's oil in the ground,

00:07:10.635 --> 00:07:12.650
it's not in South Africa
where there are diamond mines.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:14.139
He said, "The wealthiest place

00:07:14.139 --> 00:07:17.057
on the planet is the cemetery."

00:07:17.057 --> 00:07:20.214
Because there you'll find
greatness that we've never seen.

00:07:20.214 --> 00:07:22.414
There you'll find talent and genius

00:07:22.414 --> 00:07:25.637
and potential never actualized.

00:07:25.637 --> 00:07:27.771
Perhaps that's why Henry
David Thoreau wrote the words,

00:07:27.771 --> 00:07:29.554
"Oh God, to reach the point of death

00:07:29.554 --> 00:07:32.954
"only to realize that you've never lived."

00:07:32.954 --> 00:07:35.521
Maybe that's why some unknown
writer wrote the words,

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.754
"What if you live your whole life

00:07:37.754 --> 00:07:40.837
"only to discover that it was wrong?"

00:07:43.486 --> 00:07:45.553
That it was wrong.

00:07:45.553 --> 00:07:49.053
That you were chosen to do something else,

00:07:51.362 --> 00:07:53.087
and you didn't do it.

00:07:53.087 --> 00:07:54.853
And as you begin to challenge yourself,

00:07:54.853 --> 00:07:56.497
you'll discover some things about yourself

00:07:56.497 --> 00:07:58.521
that you don't know right now.

00:07:58.521 --> 00:08:00.519
The other thing is you
begin to look at yourself,

00:08:00.519 --> 00:08:03.669
look at your dreams, and
begin again to experiment.

00:08:03.669 --> 00:08:05.952
And stepping into your greatness,

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:07.519
one of the things that's very important,

00:08:07.519 --> 00:08:09.385
whatever goals and dreams that you have,

00:08:09.385 --> 00:08:10.845
repeat after me please:

00:08:10.845 --> 00:08:12.994
"Make your move before you're ready."

00:08:12.994 --> 00:08:15.144
- [Crowd] Make your move
before you're ready.

00:08:15.144 --> 00:08:15.977
- Yeah, Price Pritchett,

00:08:15.977 --> 00:08:19.134
who's a great motivator and trainer,

00:08:19.134 --> 00:08:20.995
he said, "Make your move
before you're ready."

00:08:20.995 --> 00:08:24.328
We're instructed in life to walk by faith

00:08:24.328 --> 00:08:25.402
and not by sight.

00:08:25.402 --> 00:08:28.218
So you want to really
begin to stretch yourself,

00:08:28.218 --> 00:08:29.702
you want to become a risk taker.

00:08:29.702 --> 00:08:31.885
You want to raise the bar on yourself.

00:08:31.885 --> 00:08:33.545
Most people won't do that.

00:08:33.545 --> 00:08:36.930
See, most people engage
in low life living.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:38.794
Low-risk living.

00:08:38.794 --> 00:08:40.827
This guy said, "If you're
not willing to risk,

00:08:40.827 --> 00:08:42.068
"you cannot grow."

00:08:42.068 --> 00:08:44.834
And if you cannot grow, you
cannot become your best.

00:08:44.834 --> 00:08:48.646
And if you cannot become your
best, you can't be happy.

00:08:48.646 --> 00:08:53.099
And if you can't be happy,
then what else is there?

00:08:53.099 --> 00:08:54.174
I like what Helen Keller said.

00:08:54.174 --> 00:08:56.147
"Life is short and unpredictable.

00:08:56.147 --> 00:08:57.823
"Eat the dessert first."

00:08:57.823 --> 00:09:00.093
(laughter)

00:09:00.093 --> 00:09:02.233
And so, you want to begin
to take some chances.

00:09:02.233 --> 00:09:04.009
You want to begin to challenge yourself

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:07.317
and make it okay to fail and
learn from your failures.

00:09:07.317 --> 00:09:09.067
Don't allow

00:09:09.067 --> 00:09:10.317
fear of failure

00:09:11.888 --> 00:09:14.478
and the allure, the attractiveness

00:09:14.478 --> 00:09:18.289
of playing it safe in life to draw you in.

00:09:18.289 --> 00:09:19.699
You can't get out of life alive.

00:09:19.699 --> 00:09:21.909
You've got to die to leave here.

00:09:21.909 --> 00:09:24.927
There're a lot of people
who're biting their fingers

00:09:24.927 --> 00:09:28.260
in fear that they might lose their jobs.

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:33.404
But there're few people who
have decided within themselves,

00:09:33.404 --> 00:09:35.503
"I'm going to make it."

00:09:35.503 --> 00:09:38.243
Some people aren't waiting to be cut.

00:09:38.243 --> 00:09:41.258
Some people are moving on their own,

00:09:41.258 --> 00:09:44.898
because they feel within themselves,

00:09:44.898 --> 00:09:48.538
"I've got what it takes to make it."

00:09:48.538 --> 00:09:51.107
They're not afraid about tomorrow,

00:09:51.107 --> 00:09:53.341
because of how they see themselves,

00:09:53.341 --> 00:09:56.241
because of what they
feel that they deserve,

00:09:56.241 --> 00:09:57.307
because of what they feel

00:09:57.307 --> 00:09:59.698
that they can create for themselves,

00:09:59.698 --> 00:10:02.132
because these people have decided,

00:10:02.132 --> 00:10:05.697
as they look at the future,
as they look at themselves,

00:10:05.697 --> 00:10:07.266
"There's a way.

00:10:07.266 --> 00:10:08.681
"Where there's a will, there's a way

00:10:08.681 --> 00:10:12.891
"for me to begin to create
a way out of no way."

00:10:12.891 --> 00:10:15.214
And when you have that
kind of consciousness,

00:10:15.214 --> 00:10:17.997
when you have that kind of spirit,

00:10:17.997 --> 00:10:20.302
nothing can stop you.

00:10:20.302 --> 00:10:21.135
Nothing.

00:10:22.666 --> 00:10:25.284
What would your life be like,

00:10:25.284 --> 00:10:26.894
